# Component Rules

- Use function components and keep them focused on a single UI concern.
- Use Next.js `<Image>` instead of plain `<img>` tags.
- Use Next.js `<Link>` for internal navigation instead of plain `<a>`.
- Components in `app/` should stay server-rendered unless client behavior is required.
- For the process page, keep `app/process/page.tsx` thin and render section components from `components/process/`.
- Keep section-specific logic inside the section component instead of creating broad shared abstractions too early.
- When using `@tschappaugh/mill-creek-ui`, pass required ReactNode props from the app side rather than reimplementing library components.
